[enum_1100]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,A simple plaque, bearing the name of the deceased.<br><br>(Everyone has this by default.)
val=1,A dignified little flag flutters in the breeze.
val=2,A simple little gravestone.
val=3,An ornately carved gravestone.
val=4,An elaborate font. As water collects in the bowl, it symbolises new life and hope.
val=5,A monolithic memorial stone bearing a selection of emblems.
val=6,The four-pointed star is universally recognised as the symbol of Saradomin.
val=7,This serpentine sigil represents the ruthless Zamorak.
val=8,Favoured by humans of a mystical or druidic inclination.
val=9,Followers of Bandos are now scarce, but this symbol is still used by those who remember that violent god.
val=10,Armadyl's love of winged creatures is represented by this elegant symbol. Little else is remembered of him.
val=11,Adventurers often request this symbol, although its origin and meaning have become obscure in the centuries since the god wars.
val=12,The ultimate marker for a grave, this statue evokes intimations of mortality in all who are faced with it.
val=13,The dwarves of Keldagrim are said to be the world's greatest sculptors, and a gravestone of dwarven design is an unparallelled work of art.
defaultstring=

